  "detail": "`ciSignature` now runs `redactCredentials(logLines(redactCredentials(log)).join('\\n'))`, two passes over the entire job log, to protect a multiline credential at a window boundary. `redactCredentials` costs one split/join per registered value, and a daemon holds hundreds after a day of uptime (every agent-test session and worker claim registers one). Measured with this branch's `ciSignature` on a 5 MB log with 600 registered credentials: 635 ms per call, against 4 ms on main, all synchronous in the GitHub poller on the daemon's event loop, for every failing check each time it is inspected. The daemon already stalls for seconds under load (#690, #700), and this adds to it. Required: redact only what is published, the chosen line and the excerpt window, after widening the window by the longest registered credential variant minus one character on each side, so a credential crossing the window edge is still replaced before cutting. Then cut to the final bounds. Keep the security scan (`securityFailure`) as it is. Add a test: a credential (including one with a newline) that straddles the window edge is redacted in both the line and the excerpt, and the redaction work is limited to the window, not the whole log (for example, by asserting on the length of the text passed to `redactCredentials`)."
 }
]
